<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">André Rigaud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1761">1761</a>–<a href="/years/1811">1811</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">André Rigaud was a leader of the free people of colour in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-revolution">Haitian Revolution</a>. He fought the British occupation in the 1790s but lost the War of the Knives against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toussaint-louverture">Toussaint Louverture</a> in 1799–1800 and went into exile. Returning in 1810, he set up the State of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> in opposition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandre-petion">Alexandre Pétion</a> and died the next year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andre-rigaud.jpg" alt="André Rigaud" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andr%C3%A9_Rigaud.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
